### Summary

It would be nice to have an option to display the `st.segmented_control` element vertically. Right know, I'm using a little bit of CSS to achieve that (see below). However, whenever the segmented control changes, my scroll position within the element is reset.

```css
.st-key-vertical-segmented-control [data-baseweb="button-group"] {
    flex-direction: column;
    flex-wrap: initial;
    max-height: 200px;
    max-width: 100%;
    overflow: auto;
    border: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.1);
    gap: 0;
    border-radius: .3em;
    padding: 1px;
}

.st-key-vertical-segmented-control [data-baseweb="button-group"] button {
    border-radius: 0;
    border: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.1);
}

.st-key-vertical-segmented-control [data-baseweb="button-group"] button:hover {
    background: rgba(0,0,0,.03);
    outline: 1px solid rgb(29, 52, 93);
}

.st-key-vertical-segmented-control [data-baseweb="button-group"] button[kind="segmented_controlActive"] {
    outline: 1px solid rgb(29, 52, 93);
}

.stSpinner > div {
    justify-content: center;
}
```

<img width="1467" height="614" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/31df5e0b-6d7d-40aa-83ec-5db43b4ea66b" />


### Why?

It looks nicer when there are multiple options and helps to prevent layout shift when the element options change dynamically, like when implementing interactive filter options.

### How?

Via a new parameter passed to `st.segmented_control`. Something like `layout="vertical"` or `height=200`.

